# ADR 0011: HealthKit permissions requested lazily, per feature

**Date:** 2026-08-02
**Status:** Accepted

## Context
HealthKit requires separate permissions per data type (workouts, 
body mass, heart rate, dietary energy, etc.). Requesting everything 
upfront during onboarding is high-friction and gives users no 
context for why permissions are being asked.

## Decision
Request each HealthKit permission at the point of first use for its 
feature:
- Workout permission when the user starts their first session.
- Body mass read when the user first opens the body weight view.
- Dietary permissions when Nutrition ships (v2).

## Alternatives considered
- **Upfront bulk request during onboarding:** Higher denial rate; 
  users don't understand the ask.

## Consequences
- Every HealthKit-touching feature needs to handle "not authorised" 
  as a state.
- HealthKit denials are silent (API returns empty data). Empty 
  states must handle "no data" and "denied" identically.
- If denied, users must grant in iOS Settings; empty states should 
  hint at this.
